WEBVTT

00:30.572 --> 00:31.990
This is horrible.

00:32.615 --> 00:35.243
What kind of fight could have led to this?

00:43.084 --> 00:44.210
Found them!

00:44.294 --> 00:46.796
Guys, come here!

00:46.880 --> 00:48.757
They're here!

00:50.800 --> 00:55.055
Great! They defeated an Upper Rank!

00:57.599 --> 00:58.725
Master Kagaya!

00:59.476 --> 01:00.477
A hundred years…

01:01.102 --> 01:03.938
Our situation remained unchanged
for a hundred years,

01:04.898 --> 01:06.649
but now it has changed!

01:07.067 --> 01:09.736
Do you understand? This is an omen.

01:11.362 --> 01:13.782
Fate is starting to change dramatically.

01:14.491 --> 01:16.868
The ripples will continue to spread.

01:17.494 --> 01:20.413
It will shake the surroundings.

01:21.081 --> 01:24.459
And eventually, it will reach that man.

01:25.502 --> 01:27.045
Muzan Kibutsuji,

01:27.712 --> 01:33.259
we will definitely defeat you
within our generation.

01:33.968 --> 01:37.555
You are the only disgrace
to our entire family.

02:34.028 --> 02:36.239
THREE

02:36.322 --> 02:41.995
UPPER

02:50.420 --> 02:54.007
This is the Infinity Castle.

02:55.133 --> 02:57.385
The fact I have been summoned here, means…

02:58.636 --> 03:01.055
An Upper Rank was killed
by the demon hunters.

04:32.563 --> 04:38.486
Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba
Swordsmith Village Arc

04:47.328 --> 04:50.081
Well, well. If it isn't Sir Akaza?

05:00.758 --> 05:04.095
Oh my, I'm glad to see you're well.

05:04.178 --> 05:07.348
It's been about 90 years, hasn't it?

05:09.517 --> 05:13.021
UPPER FIVE
GYOKKO

05:13.396 --> 05:18.651
My heart would jump out to think
you might have been defeated--

05:20.611 --> 05:23.948
My chest was tight from worrying.

05:29.203 --> 05:31.914
How horrifying. How horrifying.

05:31.998 --> 05:37.587
We haven't seen each other for a while,
and now Gyokko can't even count.

05:37.670 --> 05:39.172
UPPER FOUR
HANTENGU

05:39.255 --> 05:42.550
It's been 113 years
since the last summons.

05:43.342 --> 05:47.138
An indivisible number.
The half is ominous.

05:48.222 --> 05:49.432
An odd number!

05:49.515 --> 05:51.726
How horrifying! How horrifying!

05:52.268 --> 05:56.064
Biwa player, is Lord Muzan here?

05:58.524 --> 06:00.651
He has not arrived yet.

06:01.736 --> 06:03.988
Then where is Upper One?

06:05.073 --> 06:07.784
Don't tell me he's been defeated.

06:08.326 --> 06:09.911
Oh my…

06:13.539 --> 06:16.542
Wait a second, Sir Akaza.

06:19.587 --> 06:22.173
Aren't you worried about me?

06:22.965 --> 06:26.302
I was incredibly worried about you guys.

06:26.385 --> 06:28.387
You guys are my important comrades,
after all.

06:28.930 --> 06:31.849
I don't want any one of you to die.

06:33.768 --> 06:34.977
Sir Doma.

06:35.812 --> 06:37.730
UPPER TWO
DOMA

06:37.814 --> 06:40.608
Hey! Long time no see, Gyokko.

06:41.150 --> 06:44.570
Is that your new vase? Very pretty.

06:45.571 --> 06:49.367
I put a woman's freshly severed head
in the vase you gave me and used it

06:49.909 --> 06:51.119
to decorate my room.

06:52.036 --> 06:55.331
That wasn't something to keep
a severed head.

06:55.414 --> 06:58.084
But that's all right too.

06:58.626 --> 07:01.629
Right, come visit my place sometime.

07:02.171 --> 07:03.172
Get your arm…

07:05.216 --> 07:07.260
Get your arm off me.

07:23.025 --> 07:24.527
Nice punch.

07:25.111 --> 07:28.906
I guess you've became
a bit stronger than before, Sir Akaza.

07:33.619 --> 07:37.540
Upper One was called first.

07:38.291 --> 07:40.376
He's been over there the whole time.

07:47.842 --> 07:49.927
I am right here.

07:50.011 --> 07:52.638
UPPER ONE
KOKUSHIBO

07:53.222 --> 07:55.766
Lord Muzan has arrived.

08:24.837 --> 08:26.756
Gyutaro is dead.

08:28.007 --> 08:30.176
The number of Upper Ranks has decreased.

08:36.265 --> 08:40.728
Is it true, My Lord? Oh, my apologies.

08:41.521 --> 08:43.981
Since I was the one
who brought Gyutaro in,

08:44.690 --> 08:46.859
how shall I make amends?

08:47.276 --> 08:49.779
Shall I gouge out my eyeballs?

08:50.446 --> 08:51.280
Or…

08:51.364 --> 08:54.825
I don't need your eyeballs.

08:58.287 --> 09:00.831
I knew Gyutaro would lose.

09:01.499 --> 09:04.877
As I expected, Daki was a hindrance.

09:05.628 --> 09:06.879
ITEM 133

09:09.382 --> 09:13.052
If Gyutaro had fought by himself
from the beginning, he would have won.

09:14.554 --> 09:18.558
He shouldn't have fought
after poisoning them…

09:20.601 --> 09:21.435
No.

09:23.229 --> 09:25.231
Now it doesn't matter.

09:32.780 --> 09:34.240
You're all good for nothing.

09:36.242 --> 09:40.871
Those who keep
the most human parts will lose.

09:44.250 --> 09:46.669
But that's fine.

09:47.920 --> 09:51.090
I don't expect much from you anyway.

09:57.847 --> 10:01.642
You're saying such sad things again.

10:02.143 --> 10:06.731
Have I ever failed to meet
your expectations?

10:10.610 --> 10:14.614
You still haven't annihilated
the Ubuyashiki Family.

10:16.073 --> 10:18.659
And what about the Blue Spider Lily?

10:29.670 --> 10:33.007
Why hasn't it been found
even after hundreds of years?

10:37.595 --> 10:44.143
I no longer know why you even exist.

10:49.982 --> 10:53.694
Please forgive us! Please!

10:57.490 --> 10:59.325
I have no excuses to make.

11:00.618 --> 11:05.790
The Ubuyashiki Family
is hiding skillfully.

11:07.083 --> 11:10.878
I'm not good at detecting and searching.

11:11.462 --> 11:13.172
So what can I do?

11:14.382 --> 11:18.260
Lord Muzan, I'm different from them!

11:18.344 --> 11:25.351
I have information that will bring you
one step closer to what you want.

11:25.434 --> 11:27.186
Just now, I…

11:28.687 --> 11:31.774
I detest change.

11:35.236 --> 11:37.071
Changing circumstances.

11:37.154 --> 11:38.739
Changes of the physique.

11:39.323 --> 11:40.825
Changing emotions.

11:41.784 --> 11:45.079
Every change causes degradation.

11:45.621 --> 11:46.997
Becoming waning.

11:47.623 --> 11:49.875
I love eternality.

11:50.501 --> 11:54.672
To be perfect and forever unchanged.

11:58.175 --> 12:02.012
Lord Muzan's hand is touching my head.

12:02.096 --> 12:04.849
Nice. Very nice.

12:10.396 --> 12:14.525
For the first time in 113 years,
an Upper Rank was killed.

12:15.651 --> 12:18.279
It displeases me immensely.

12:23.826 --> 12:29.457
Don't try to gleefully pass on information
that hasn't been confirmed yet.

12:37.465 --> 12:41.218
From now on, you must work
with greater desperation.

12:42.428 --> 12:48.142
It seems I have been spoiling you
because you are Upper Ranks.

12:49.351 --> 12:52.897
Gyokko, after you have confirmed
the information,

12:52.980 --> 12:55.649
go there with Hantengu.

13:06.118 --> 13:07.953
As you wish.

13:13.501 --> 13:17.463
Why? It was the information I got.

13:17.546 --> 13:19.215
So unfair!

13:21.133 --> 13:23.594
But that's what I adore about him.

13:26.931 --> 13:30.893
Sir Gyokko! What information do you keep?

13:32.937 --> 13:35.064
I want to go too.

13:35.147 --> 13:37.525
Well, that's…

13:41.237 --> 13:43.239
Won't you tell me?

13:43.906 --> 13:44.865
I'm begging--

13:49.328 --> 13:52.831
Did Lord Muzan give you an order?

13:54.250 --> 13:55.167
Get lost.

14:01.257 --> 14:02.258
Akaza.

14:03.926 --> 14:05.970
You've gone too far.

14:09.598 --> 14:11.850
It's all right, Sir Kokushibo.

14:13.936 --> 14:15.771
I don't mind at all.

14:16.397 --> 14:19.233
I am not saying this for your sake.

14:20.317 --> 14:22.027
It disturbs the ranking.

14:23.112 --> 14:29.785
I'm even worried about cracks
that might appear in the hierarchy.

14:35.082 --> 14:37.167
Oh, I see.

14:38.002 --> 14:38.961
Akaza.

14:40.004 --> 14:46.051
If you don't like it, then request
a bloody battle to replace us.

14:46.385 --> 14:50.139
But, Sir Kokushibo…

14:50.764 --> 14:55.477
Even if he makes that request,
Sir Akaza can't beat us.

14:56.103 --> 15:00.482
Moreover, in my case, I became
a demon later than Sir Akaza,

15:00.566 --> 15:05.571
and I rose quickly through the ranks,
so he must be mad at me.

15:06.155 --> 15:07.448
Please understand that.

15:10.200 --> 15:14.455
Besides, I purposely didn't dodge.

15:14.955 --> 15:16.582
I was just playing around a bit.

15:16.665 --> 15:20.085
This is how you get along with each other.

15:20.711 --> 15:24.924
We must be lenient with those
ranked below us, not scorn the--

15:25.007 --> 15:26.091
Akaza.

15:31.263 --> 15:37.061
Do you understand what I am saying to you?

15:42.775 --> 15:43.984
I understand.

15:47.988 --> 15:51.450
I'll definitely kill you.

15:57.998 --> 15:59.333
Is that so?

16:00.584 --> 16:02.044
You have my encouragement.

16:09.051 --> 16:12.554
Goodbye, Sir Kokushibo! Goodbye!

16:15.182 --> 16:20.396
I kinda feel like I wasn't included
in their conversation.

16:20.771 --> 16:23.399
I'm overthinking it, aren't I, Sir Akaza?

16:27.319 --> 16:29.321
Sir Akaza!

16:30.531 --> 16:34.451
-Aren't we in the middle of talking?
-Quietly and slowly…

16:36.662 --> 16:41.458
Send me and Hantengu to the same place!

16:46.588 --> 16:48.340
Wait! Me, too!

16:55.055 --> 16:57.391
Hey, biwa player.

16:58.726 --> 17:00.728
How about going to my--

17:01.645 --> 17:03.188
I refuse.

17:10.738 --> 17:13.198
They're no fun.

17:15.701 --> 17:18.787
Lord Founder,
believers are here to see you.

17:19.413 --> 17:21.081
Oh, really?

17:21.165 --> 17:22.875
Sorry for the wait.

17:23.625 --> 17:24.543
Oopsie-daisy…

17:25.294 --> 17:27.671
I'm going to put this on my head first.

17:29.089 --> 17:30.299
I'm ready.

17:31.091 --> 17:32.426
Please let them in.

17:36.472 --> 17:37.681
I made tea for you.

17:39.016 --> 17:41.101
Oh, thank you.

17:42.728 --> 17:45.439
He sure sleeps well.

17:46.732 --> 17:50.444
Sorry, it appears
my wife also fell asleep.

17:51.570 --> 17:56.450
I'm really sorry to make
a guest babysit our child.

17:57.826 --> 17:58.827
I don't mind it.

17:59.787 --> 18:00.871
She must be exhausted.

18:01.830 --> 18:04.374
Giving birth and raising a child is hard.

18:08.212 --> 18:10.005
I'll leave after I drink this.

18:11.381 --> 18:14.343
I can't bear to keep eating for free.

18:14.968 --> 18:18.555
Don't say that! You saved our lives.

18:18.639 --> 18:23.102
Without you, let alone us,
this child wouldn't have been born.

18:28.148 --> 18:29.149
I understand.

18:29.817 --> 18:33.237
Then at least,
I'll tell my descendants about you.

18:34.238 --> 18:35.114
It's not necessary.

18:36.281 --> 18:40.744
Still, you must be in trouble
because you have no heirs.

18:41.537 --> 18:43.997
I'm just a charcoal seller,
I know I may not be able to do it,

18:44.081 --> 18:45.457
but one day someone will…

18:46.416 --> 18:47.751
It's not necessary.

18:48.460 --> 18:49.294
Sumiyoshi.

18:52.464 --> 18:57.177
Those who master their path
always end up in the same place.

18:58.637 --> 19:03.100
Even if the time changes
or the way to get there is different,

19:04.309 --> 19:06.145
they are certain to reach the same place.

19:08.981 --> 19:13.861
You seem to think I'm someone special.

19:14.570 --> 19:15.779
But I'm not.

19:19.283 --> 19:22.536
I cannot protect anything important to me,

19:23.412 --> 19:27.166
and I have failed to do
what I should have done in my life.

19:29.334 --> 19:31.670
I am a man without value.

19:34.798 --> 19:36.008
Please…

19:36.091 --> 19:38.177
Please don't talk like that.

19:39.178 --> 19:43.098
I beg you, don't belittle yourself.

19:44.349 --> 19:45.350
It's sad.

19:46.351 --> 19:47.352
So sad.

19:59.531 --> 20:01.533
Was that a dream?

20:11.376 --> 20:12.502
Where is this?

20:13.795 --> 20:14.713
Where am I?

20:18.383 --> 20:19.426
Are you all right?

20:19.509 --> 20:23.138
You've been unconscious
for two months after the battle.

20:25.224 --> 20:27.309
Is that so?

20:28.477 --> 20:29.895
I see.

20:34.066 --> 20:37.319
I'm glad you're awake.

20:40.405 --> 20:44.952
Episode 1: Someone's Dream

20:49.456 --> 20:51.458
My name is Goto.

20:52.292 --> 20:55.837
I'm a Kakushi in the clean-up crew
of the Demon Slayer Corps.

20:57.256 --> 21:00.008
During the Hashira meeting,
the one who told Tanjiro Kamado,

21:00.092 --> 21:03.428
"How long are you gonna sleep?
Get up already!"

21:03.512 --> 21:04.346
…was me.

21:04.429 --> 21:05.973
GOTO THE KAKUSHI

21:06.056 --> 21:07.975
I have a fateful connection with him.

21:09.726 --> 21:11.019
I'm also the one who found them

21:11.103 --> 21:13.146
in the Entertainment District
two months ago.

21:14.481 --> 21:16.024
They were in such a state.

21:16.984 --> 21:18.777
They're getting along, aren't they?

21:19.569 --> 21:21.655
That's what I thought, but those three

21:21.738 --> 21:23.448
were unconscious
and in critical condition.

21:24.741 --> 21:27.244
I truly respect them
who are younger than me,

21:27.327 --> 21:30.831
and became swordsmen
and fight for their lives.

21:32.207 --> 21:34.334
I don't get this guy. Who is he anyway?

21:36.503 --> 21:40.632
And now, I'm carrying
fine castella in my hands.

21:41.758 --> 21:45.929
To be honest, I'm doing my best
to not eat it myself right now.

21:46.888 --> 21:49.933
It's a gift for him
who still hasn't regained consciousness.

21:50.809 --> 21:53.937
They say he has a good nose,
maybe this will wake him up.

22:02.029 --> 22:03.947
Clean this up, good God.

22:04.281 --> 22:06.658
Seriously, Kanao?
You leave everything undone.

22:06.742 --> 22:07.701
METSU

22:07.784 --> 22:09.661
She's a weird girl who doesn't talk.

22:09.745 --> 22:12.539
It's because they made her join
the Corps at such a young age.

22:14.291 --> 22:16.418
Well, she outranks me,
so I can't complain.

22:17.085 --> 22:18.420
Even though I'm 23 years old.

22:21.173 --> 22:23.717
I'm putting the castella here.

22:23.800 --> 22:25.510
You can eat it after a while,

22:26.094 --> 22:28.013
or if it looks like it's going bad.

22:29.097 --> 22:32.225
Oh, thank you.

22:36.813 --> 22:39.232
He's awake, isn't he?

22:39.316 --> 22:41.485
You should be more excited!

22:41.568 --> 22:43.737
All you can do is stay silent?

22:43.820 --> 22:47.282
You should call someone!
And say he's woken up!

22:47.824 --> 22:49.242
You dummy!

22:50.118 --> 22:51.995
Everyone is worried!

22:52.079 --> 22:54.998
At times like this, ranks don't matter!

22:57.375 --> 23:00.170
Kiyo! Sumi! Naho!

23:00.253 --> 23:01.713
Aoi!

23:01.797 --> 23:05.008
Tanjiro has regained consciousness!

23:05.092 --> 23:06.843
ABDOMINAL BREATHING

23:11.431 --> 23:13.141
I'm glad!

23:13.225 --> 23:14.935
I'll give you my red bean bun.

23:15.018 --> 23:16.978
The castella are scattered.

23:23.485 --> 23:26.113
A ghost!

23:28.865 --> 23:32.369
Oh… It's Aoi tangled up in the laundry.

23:33.328 --> 23:35.789
I'm glad you woke up!

23:35.872 --> 23:39.167
You went on my behalf,
and you all got hurt!

23:41.753 --> 23:43.255
Thank you.

23:44.131 --> 23:47.384
What about everyone else?
Are they all right?

23:48.510 --> 23:51.012
That yellow-headed one…
Was it two days ago?

23:51.096 --> 23:51.972
Yup!

23:52.055 --> 23:55.183
He's active again.
I heard he's on a mission.

23:55.267 --> 23:56.434
Reluctantly.

23:56.518 --> 24:00.063
Zenitsu woke up the next day.

24:02.023 --> 24:07.028
The Sound Hashira was walking on his own,
leaning on his wives' shoulders though.

24:07.112 --> 24:09.948
It hurts! This is irritating.

24:10.615 --> 24:13.660
The Kakushis were pulling themselves,
seeing how tough he is.

24:14.995 --> 24:16.371
They were incredibly shocked.

24:16.454 --> 24:19.207
He's scary. He can still stand.

24:19.749 --> 24:20.959
Really scary.

24:21.042 --> 24:22.961
Aren't his injuries pretty serious?

24:24.504 --> 24:25.630
Glad to hear.

24:26.965 --> 24:28.133
And Inosuke?

24:28.216 --> 24:31.303
He was also in danger for a while.

24:32.846 --> 24:36.183
Inosuke's condition was really bad.

24:36.266 --> 24:40.187
He was slow to use breathing to stop
the bleeding because of the poison.

24:41.438 --> 24:42.856
I see.

24:42.939 --> 24:48.445
In that case, I must be hallucinating,
seeing him clinging to the ceiling.

24:53.617 --> 24:55.160
What the heck are you doing?

24:56.995 --> 24:58.997
Good job noticing me, Tanpachiro!

25:00.207 --> 25:03.084
You see, I'm lying on my back.

25:06.463 --> 25:09.633
I'm the man who woke up
seven days before you.

25:10.759 --> 25:15.430
I'm glad. You really are amazing.

25:17.515 --> 25:18.808
Praise me more!

25:18.892 --> 25:22.646
And you're weak! Don't make me worry!

25:22.729 --> 25:25.357
You are not normal!

25:25.440 --> 25:27.234
Lady Shinobu also said that, right?

25:27.317 --> 25:31.071
Right, Tanjiro. Look at this book.

25:32.364 --> 25:35.408
It's a weasel from another country
called a honey badger.

25:35.492 --> 25:37.953
Its thick skin is like armor.

25:38.036 --> 25:40.789
It can survive even if a lion bites it.

25:40.872 --> 25:42.415
It's cute.

25:42.499 --> 25:46.253
Because poison doesn't affect it,
it even eats venomous snakes.

25:48.421 --> 25:51.800
Lady Shinobu said
Inosuke is like this animal.

25:53.093 --> 25:54.886
Lady Kocho can be sloppy, too.

25:56.137 --> 25:59.391
She may have gotten tired
of worrying about him.

25:59.849 --> 26:02.269
Wait… Get off from there!

26:03.103 --> 26:05.272
In a nutshell, I'm immortal!

26:06.773 --> 26:08.858
No, you're just a moron.

26:08.942 --> 26:11.653
Who's a moron, you bastard?

26:12.654 --> 26:14.030
Stop it!

26:14.114 --> 26:15.532
Hey, cut it out!

26:15.615 --> 26:18.702
Poison doesn't work well on you
but neither does medicine!

26:18.785 --> 26:21.871
Lady Shinobu told you
to be careful, didn't she?

26:22.455 --> 26:23.957
You forget easily.

26:24.040 --> 26:26.501
-Be quiet…
-Shut up and stop pulling on me, shrimp!

26:26.584 --> 26:29.713
What did you say?
We're almost the same height!

26:30.422 --> 26:32.841
Tanjiro fell asleep, so be quiet!

26:37.804 --> 26:39.681
He's in a coma again!

26:39.764 --> 26:42.517
Don't you dare say anything ill omens!

26:42.600 --> 26:44.060
Please be quiet!

26:44.602 --> 26:47.564
Kanao, let's make some rice gruel.

26:48.315 --> 26:49.274
Sure.

26:49.357 --> 26:53.862
I hope he recovers quickly
and can eat a lot.

27:06.249 --> 27:09.753
THANK GOODNESS…
I THOUGHT HE WAS GOING TO DIE…

27:15.759 --> 27:17.761
I'm the wind!

27:17.844 --> 27:19.262
I'm next!

27:19.346 --> 27:20.722
Then, me!

27:20.805 --> 27:24.392
Tanjiro recovered a week later.

27:28.229 --> 27:30.857
When I informed Goto of that
during his expedition,

27:30.940 --> 27:33.735
he was surprised at
how quickly Tanjiro recovered.

27:34.778 --> 27:37.739
Whoa, seriously? They really are monsters.

27:39.157 --> 27:42.744
Inosuke was back to duty soon afterwards.

27:43.828 --> 27:45.622
I'm the strongest!

27:46.664 --> 27:47.874
I'm heading out!

27:48.792 --> 27:50.960
No!

27:51.044 --> 27:54.589
It's cold! It's scary!

27:54.672 --> 27:57.092
I'm leaving!

27:57.175 --> 27:58.802
It's lonely!

27:58.885 --> 28:00.261
-About Zenitsu…
-Tanjiro!

28:00.345 --> 28:03.056
-he's going on a distant mission.
-Inosuke!

28:03.139 --> 28:04.808
-I hear from other members…
-Nezuko!

28:04.891 --> 28:06.726
-that he's complaining too much.
-Nezuko!

28:07.352 --> 28:10.271
Aoi? Are you thinking of me just now?

28:10.897 --> 28:12.565
Do you miss me? Do you want to see me?

28:12.649 --> 28:15.485
I bet you must be missing me!

28:15.568 --> 28:16.569
Shut up!

28:17.612 --> 28:22.492
Lastly, Tanjiro is doing
rehabilitation training on a daily basis.

28:30.417 --> 28:31.835
Ouch…

28:33.336 --> 28:34.796
How frustrating.

28:34.879 --> 28:37.841
I still can't seem to get
my physical strength back quickly.

28:39.467 --> 28:40.427
Oh, right.

28:40.510 --> 28:43.304
Was a sword delivered while I was asleep?

28:43.805 --> 28:45.932
The blade got chipped.

28:48.143 --> 28:50.770
A sword, huh? Sword…

28:51.354 --> 28:54.274
Mr. Haganezuka did send a letter.

28:55.191 --> 28:56.818
Do you want to read it?

28:57.610 --> 28:59.070
No sword for you.

28:59.154 --> 29:00.530
I DESPISE YOU
CURSE YOU - UNFORGIVABLE

29:01.030 --> 29:03.616
This is bad.

29:03.700 --> 29:05.702
I thought so.

29:10.999 --> 29:15.712
It's been two months,
but no sword was delivered.

29:18.214 --> 29:21.468
This time it just got chipped.

29:21.551 --> 29:24.179
I know, I broke it once before.

29:26.181 --> 29:29.642
It's not uncommon
for swords to be damaged.

29:30.268 --> 29:33.855
But Mr. Haganezuka is
a bit of a difficult man.

29:33.938 --> 29:36.566
How about going to the village?

29:37.108 --> 29:39.986
Maybe it would be best
to talk to him directly.

29:40.945 --> 29:41.905
What village?

29:41.988 --> 29:44.491
The village of the swordsmiths.

29:44.574 --> 29:46.659
Huh? Can I go there?

29:47.827 --> 29:51.998
Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba
Swordsmith Village Arc

29:56.503 --> 29:57.796
Pleased to meet you.

29:57.879 --> 30:01.716
The Master has granted permission,
so I will guide you.

30:02.342 --> 30:04.761
Pleased to meet you, too.
I'm Tanjiro Kamado.

30:05.470 --> 30:06.721
Thank you for your cooperation.

30:07.514 --> 30:10.225
I cannot give you my name
due to the circumstances,

30:10.308 --> 30:11.476
but leave it to me.

30:12.852 --> 30:13.686
Now put these on.

30:14.437 --> 30:15.396
What are these?

30:15.855 --> 30:17.398
A blindfold and earplugs.

30:18.233 --> 30:19.692
The village is hidden.

30:20.401 --> 30:24.405
-And I will carry you on my back.
-Huh?

30:25.031 --> 30:27.075
Also, since you have a good nose…

30:27.992 --> 30:29.285
Nose plugs for you.

30:29.994 --> 30:32.247
Take care!

30:33.581 --> 30:36.167
Nichirin Swords are made
in the Swordsmith Village,

30:36.251 --> 30:39.337
a very important place
for the Demon Slayer Corps.

30:40.213 --> 30:44.050
In order to prevent demons
from finding and attacking the village,

30:45.134 --> 30:48.179
no one knows its location.

30:49.889 --> 30:52.350
Of course, this woman doesn't know either.

30:53.184 --> 30:54.018
Counting on ya.

30:54.102 --> 30:54.936
Each Kakushi…

30:55.019 --> 30:56.229
-Okay!
-Leave it to me.

30:56.312 --> 30:57.897
…passes me on to the next.

30:57.981 --> 30:58.898
SWORDSMITH VILLAGE ARC
START

30:58.982 --> 31:01.609
Furthermore, they frequently
change the routes

31:01.693 --> 31:03.361
and the Kakushi along them.

31:04.237 --> 31:05.864
A Kakushi is guided…

31:05.947 --> 31:06.865
Take care of me.

31:06.948 --> 31:08.575
…to the next Kakushi by a crow

31:08.658 --> 31:11.578
which is also frequently changed as well.

31:12.245 --> 31:13.663
Take care on your way back!

31:13.746 --> 31:14.706
KAKUSHI

31:15.790 --> 31:17.083
He's a good guy.

31:18.585 --> 31:23.214
Apparently, the Master's mansion
is hidden in a more complicated way.

31:23.298 --> 31:26.175
Seriously, smart people are amazing.

31:27.468 --> 31:28.803
I'll take it off.

31:51.367 --> 31:53.161
What incredible buildings!

31:53.244 --> 31:55.914
Every visitor always says that.

31:57.999 --> 32:01.586
And this smell…
It appears to be a hot spring nearby.

32:01.669 --> 32:04.380
You're right. There is a hot spring here.

32:04.464 --> 32:07.175
You can soak there
and relieve yourself later.

32:07.258 --> 32:12.513
But before that, the Chief's house
is just to the left over there.

32:12.597 --> 32:16.184
-You should greet him first.
-Got it.

32:17.268 --> 32:18.811
Now I will take my leave.

32:19.687 --> 32:25.193
Thank you very much!

32:27.236 --> 32:29.155
…very much.

32:32.158 --> 32:34.327
I heard words of gratitude echoing.

32:42.543 --> 32:44.337
I wonder who's coming.

32:44.420 --> 32:46.547
That gets me kind of excited.

32:47.924 --> 32:48.800
Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba
Swordsmith Village Arc

32:56.641 --> 32:58.726
Greetings.

32:58.810 --> 33:03.064
I'm the chief of this village,
Tecchin Tecchikawahara.

33:03.147 --> 33:04.273
Nice to meet ya.

33:04.899 --> 33:09.696
Despite being the smallest, I'm the most
esteemed person in the village.

33:09.779 --> 33:14.492
So esteemed that you should bow
till your head touches the tatami mat.

33:18.496 --> 33:21.040
My name is Tanjiro Kamado.
It's a pleasure to meet you.

33:21.124 --> 33:21.958
CHIEF

33:22.375 --> 33:24.252
What a good kid.

33:24.335 --> 33:25.211
Come here.

33:25.753 --> 33:27.171
I'll give ya karinto.

33:28.339 --> 33:29.549
Thank you.

33:30.800 --> 33:32.260
It's delicious.

33:32.343 --> 33:33.302
I know, right?

33:34.387 --> 33:39.767
Regarding Hotaru, it seems
his whereabouts are unknown.

33:39.851 --> 33:42.895
We're searching for him,
so please be patient.

33:43.730 --> 33:44.564
Hotaru?

33:44.647 --> 33:47.275
Yes, Hotaru Haganezuka.

33:47.358 --> 33:49.152
That's a cute name.

33:49.235 --> 33:52.488
I know, right?
I was the one who named him.

33:52.572 --> 33:56.701
He told me it was too cute
and he cursed me.

33:56.784 --> 33:57.994
That's sad.

34:00.121 --> 34:03.332
He's been like that since he was little.

34:03.416 --> 34:06.502
He throws tantrums
and goes off to sulk somewhere.

34:06.586 --> 34:07.920
Sorry.

34:08.004 --> 34:09.088
Please don't apologize!

34:09.172 --> 34:12.592
It's because I broke the sword
and chipped the blade.

34:13.092 --> 34:14.677
No. That's wrong.

34:16.179 --> 34:20.808
It's his fault for making
dull blades that break.

34:23.352 --> 34:27.607
We'll bring him to you as soon
as we find him, so don't worry.

34:28.191 --> 34:29.901
Yeah, true.

34:30.568 --> 34:32.862
Uh-oh, don't be too rough.

34:33.488 --> 34:39.327
I heard you haven't yet recovered
enough to go demon hunting.

34:39.952 --> 34:43.664
If Hotaru doesn't forge you a sword
by the time you're ready,

34:43.748 --> 34:46.417
I'll appoint another swordsmith for you.

34:47.877 --> 34:51.798
Our village hot spring is good
for healing the body.

34:51.881 --> 34:54.467
Just relax and take your time.

34:56.385 --> 34:57.470
I'll guide you there.

34:59.806 --> 35:01.724
I hope they don't fight.

35:10.942 --> 35:14.654
There are swordsmiths and workshops
all over this village.

35:17.198 --> 35:20.326
That's how your swords are made.

35:24.080 --> 35:27.792
It's thanks to swordsmiths here
that we are able to wield our swords.

35:28.543 --> 35:29.710
Thank you!

35:30.336 --> 35:32.547
Don't mind it. It's our job.

35:32.630 --> 35:34.173
You don't need to thank us.

35:36.759 --> 35:38.427
The hot spring is up this hill.

35:39.011 --> 35:41.264
It can heal many kinds of wounds.

35:41.347 --> 35:45.601
Cuts, burns, hemorrhoids,
anal fistula, and constipation.

35:45.685 --> 35:49.147
It even can heal everything
from gout to the pain of losing your love.

35:49.230 --> 35:51.107
Please take your time to bathe.

35:51.774 --> 35:55.319
-Got it.
-I'll be down here preparing your meal.

35:55.862 --> 35:57.446
Yes, thank you.

36:02.785 --> 36:04.453
It's Tanjiro!

36:04.537 --> 36:07.373
Tanjiro!

36:07.456 --> 36:08.708
Watch out!

36:09.125 --> 36:12.378
Please be careful!
Your breasts are about to spill out!

36:16.007 --> 36:18.718
-Hey, listen! Listen!
-Watch out!

36:20.428 --> 36:24.182
Geez! Someone ignored me!

36:24.265 --> 36:27.351
I said hello, but he ignored me!

36:27.435 --> 36:28.686
Who did?

36:28.769 --> 36:30.688
I don't know!

36:31.147 --> 36:34.025
I asked his name, but he ignored me!

36:34.108 --> 36:37.320
Don't you think it's terrible?
I'm a Hashira, you know!

36:37.403 --> 36:41.157
All the good feelings from
soaking are already ruined!

36:41.240 --> 36:43.868
It looks like dinner will be ready soon.

36:43.951 --> 36:45.536
It's rice with matsutake mushrooms.

36:47.121 --> 36:48.414
Really?

36:49.123 --> 36:53.044
-Dinner! Rice with matsutake mushrooms!
-I guess she's a big eater.

36:55.546 --> 36:57.465
Whoa! It's huge!

36:58.299 --> 36:59.300
Aw…

37:01.510 --> 37:02.386
A front tooth?

37:02.887 --> 37:04.931
Did someone lose a tooth?

37:11.520 --> 37:13.439
A guy with his head shaved on the sides.

37:15.399 --> 37:18.611
If I remember, Sumi told me his name.

37:19.695 --> 37:20.905
Genya Shinazugawa!

37:22.490 --> 37:23.491
Go die!

37:32.667 --> 37:35.169
Long time no see! How have you been?

37:35.253 --> 37:37.171
You have the same surname
as the Wind Hashira!

37:40.299 --> 37:42.510
Don't talk to me!

37:45.513 --> 37:49.225
I thought we could get closer
by soaking together.

37:49.308 --> 37:51.435
Human relations are difficult.

37:55.189 --> 37:56.649
You're amazing!

37:57.066 --> 38:00.861
Do you think so?
But I didn't eat that much today.

38:00.945 --> 38:03.030
I'll eat a lot, too, and get strong.

38:03.656 --> 38:04.949
Oh, right.

38:05.032 --> 38:07.868
The boy you met at the hot spring
was Genya Shinazugawa.

38:07.952 --> 38:10.037
We joined the Corps at the same time.

38:11.205 --> 38:12.790
You don't say!

38:13.416 --> 38:15.793
He must be Shinazugawa's younger brother.

38:15.876 --> 38:19.046
But he said he doesn't have a brother.

38:19.588 --> 38:21.299
I wonder if they don't get along.

38:21.382 --> 38:22.800
That's so sad.

38:22.883 --> 38:25.845
Yeah, I wonder why.

38:29.348 --> 38:31.392
What's the matter, Nezuko?

38:31.475 --> 38:33.019
Take this.

38:34.312 --> 38:37.898
My family has five kids including me,
and we all get along.

38:37.982 --> 38:42.570
I don't really understand, but I think
the Shinazugawa brothers are scary.

38:43.154 --> 38:45.364
Genya hasn't come yet.

38:45.448 --> 38:46.866
-You're so cute!
-It'd be nice

38:46.949 --> 38:48.200
if we can talk to him a little.

38:49.744 --> 38:51.370
I don't think he'll come.

38:51.996 --> 38:54.874
One of the villagers said
he doesn't take a meal at all.

38:55.708 --> 38:57.543
Did he bring his own food?

38:58.753 --> 39:00.004
I wonder if he's all right.

39:00.588 --> 39:02.381
I'll bring him some rice balls later.

39:03.507 --> 39:05.259
Nice idea. Let's do that.

39:07.678 --> 39:09.638
Hey, Nezuko, hear this.

39:10.806 --> 39:16.270
When I saw the rice balls,
I got hungry again.

39:16.354 --> 39:17.730
Don't tell anyone, okay?

39:19.899 --> 39:22.985
Why did you join
the Demon Slayer Corps, Kanroji?

39:24.445 --> 39:25.488
Me?

39:26.197 --> 39:27.907
It's embarrassing.

39:27.990 --> 39:30.659
Do you really want to know?

39:30.743 --> 39:31.660
Well…

39:32.828 --> 39:36.707
I'm trying to find a man to marry!

39:36.999 --> 39:40.336
Every girl wants to find
someone stronger than herself.

39:40.419 --> 39:41.837
We wanted to be protected.

39:41.921 --> 39:45.383
Do you understand my feelings?
Maybe it's difficult for boys.

39:45.466 --> 39:47.176
I mean, the Hashiras are strong, right?

39:47.259 --> 39:50.471
But since I couldn't meet them,
I became a Hashira myself.

39:50.554 --> 39:52.264
I did my best, you know!

39:55.059 --> 39:56.811
Genya isn't here.

39:58.104 --> 39:59.021
Lady Kanroji.

40:00.773 --> 40:03.109
Your sword will soon
be finished being sharpened.

40:03.943 --> 40:07.571
Please, come to the workshop
for the final adjustment.

40:08.531 --> 40:11.700
Oh my, looks like I have to go.

40:11.784 --> 40:14.453
Don't worry. I'll see you off.

40:14.537 --> 40:17.790
You don't need to.
I'll probably leave late at night.

40:19.542 --> 40:20.960
Uh, but…

40:21.794 --> 40:22.920
I see.

40:25.256 --> 40:26.215
Tanjiro.

40:27.550 --> 40:30.094
I don't know if we'll ever see
each other alive again,

40:30.553 --> 40:31.637
but let's do our best.

40:32.763 --> 40:35.683
You fought an Upper Rank Demon
and survived.

40:36.350 --> 40:38.018
That's an incredible experience.

40:39.270 --> 40:43.566
What you gain through actual experience
is worth so much more than anything.

40:44.275 --> 40:47.361
It's comparable to five years of training,
or even ten years.

40:48.070 --> 40:52.825
You are now much stronger
than you were before, Tanjiro.

40:56.203 --> 41:00.124
I, Mitsuri Kanroji, am rooting
for the Kamado siblings!

41:05.588 --> 41:07.006
Thank you very much.

41:08.007 --> 41:09.633
But I still have a long way to go.

41:10.134 --> 41:12.678
Thanks to Uzui, we were able to win.

41:13.345 --> 41:14.889
I'll work harder and harder

41:16.015 --> 41:18.267
to defeat Muzan Kibutsuji.

41:22.855 --> 41:26.567
You got permission to stay longer, right?

41:27.234 --> 41:29.153
Yeah, I suppose so.

41:34.325 --> 41:35.659
It seems, in this village,

41:35.743 --> 41:38.412
there's a secret weapon
that makes you stronger.

41:39.121 --> 41:40.206
Look for it, okay?

41:41.540 --> 41:43.083
See you again!

42:06.941 --> 42:08.567
What a treat! And it's still morning.

42:09.443 --> 42:12.112
We harvest wild vegetables
from the mountains around here.

42:12.196 --> 42:15.074
Even the fish were freshly caught
from the river this morning.

42:17.409 --> 42:22.039
The Chief will let you know
as soon as he finds Haganezuka.

42:22.665 --> 42:25.501
Until then, you can rest
and recover your strength.

42:26.168 --> 42:27.753
I understand, thank you.

42:29.630 --> 42:30.548
Let's eat.

42:35.803 --> 42:37.555
Nezuko, you see, I…

42:39.139 --> 42:43.602
I know I need to rest my body,
but while waiting for Haganezuka,

42:43.686 --> 42:45.479
I think I'll look for the secret weapon

42:45.563 --> 42:48.816
that Kanroji told me about
that will make me stronger.

42:49.400 --> 42:50.609
Do you want to come along?

42:55.823 --> 42:57.491
I wonder what kind of weapon it is.

42:59.493 --> 43:00.953
Is it a sword?

43:01.036 --> 43:02.705
Is it buried somewhere?

43:02.788 --> 43:05.165
It's exciting like on a treasure hunt.

43:07.501 --> 43:11.922
This is a great place,
but the hot spring smell is very strong.

43:14.425 --> 43:18.012
Not being completely healthy
is hampering my nose.

43:18.554 --> 43:20.806
You're so persistent!
Cut it out, will you!

43:22.683 --> 43:24.435
I should be the one saying that.

43:24.935 --> 43:27.354
We're wasting time
arguing back and forth like this.

43:28.355 --> 43:31.108
A child? And the other one is…

43:31.191 --> 43:32.568
-If I said no, it's no!
-Huh?

43:32.651 --> 43:33.902
-Go home!
-Isn't he a Hashira?

43:33.986 --> 43:36.614
-Why do I have to give it to you?
-Shinobu told me his name.

43:36.697 --> 43:39.033
-I don't care if you're a Hashira!
-Right.

43:39.116 --> 43:40.451
Now get out of here!

43:40.534 --> 43:43.120
He's Muichiro Tokito the Mist Hashira.

43:44.788 --> 43:47.916
So another Hashira came to this village.

43:49.460 --> 43:50.419
Give me the key.

43:50.919 --> 43:52.087
I won't give it to you!

43:52.171 --> 43:55.049
This is my ancestor's precious creation!

43:56.258 --> 43:58.802
Is there someone else behind that kid?

43:59.928 --> 44:02.348
I definitely won't give it to you!

44:04.516 --> 44:06.852
Is that a man?

44:08.020 --> 44:09.063
I wonder who that is.

44:13.859 --> 44:15.194
I know him.

44:15.277 --> 44:18.405
I've seen him before.

44:39.593 --> 44:42.596
Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba
Swordsmith Village Arc

48:25.110 --> 48:26.069
DEMON SLAYER: SWORDSMITH VILLAGE ARC
NO. 1

48:26.153 --> 48:27.112
CONGRATS ON SWORDSMITH VILLAGE ARC!

48:27.195 --> 48:29.615
I'm glad you're finally awake, Tanjiro.

48:29.698 --> 48:31.325
We're glad.

48:31.408 --> 48:32.618
Thank you, everyone.

48:33.201 --> 48:37.039
By the way, since when did
Inosuke cling to the ceiling?

48:42.377 --> 48:47.007
That means he's been there
for at least an hour.

48:47.090 --> 48:49.426
He's still as crazy as ever.

48:49.509 --> 48:50.802
Yup, yup.

48:50.886 --> 48:52.387
You're wrong!

48:54.222 --> 48:55.724
What do you mean, huh?

48:55.807 --> 48:58.101
I'd been there since the day before.

48:58.185 --> 48:59.728
What?

49:02.439 --> 49:04.983
Wake up! Wake up, Kanpachiro!

49:05.067 --> 49:06.735
Open your eyes!

49:06.818 --> 49:08.612
Just wake up, you piece of shit!

49:09.071 --> 49:11.156
So you had been doing that?

49:11.239 --> 49:14.743
No wonder Tanjiro could wake up.

49:14.826 --> 49:16.119
Yes, no wonder.

49:16.203 --> 49:18.121
Your mind controls your body!

49:18.205 --> 49:20.415
Inosuke, thank you so much.

49:21.750 --> 49:24.461
Next up on Episode 2:
"Yoriichi Type Zero"

49:24.544 --> 49:27.631
I'll do my best in the Swordsmith Village.

49:27.714 --> 49:28.924
Don't make me worry!

49:29.007 --> 49:31.093
TO BE CONTINUED
